nclude cases for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines, and CLI exit codes (0, 1 and 2).\nFAIL: any field wrong, any runtime dependency, tests failing or not run, or any of the five listed cases missing.\n\n## Check 5 — packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\nRun: `test -s packages/jsonl-lint/README.md && echo ok` and `grep -n 'jsonl-lint' README.md`.\nPASS: the package README exists and is non-empty, and the root `README.md` mentions `jsonl-lint` as a tool in the repo.\nFAIL: the package README is missing or empty, or the root README does not list the tool.\n\n## Check 6 — The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\nRun: `gh pr view <PR> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,state,baseRefName`; `gh pr checks <PR> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test`; and at the PR head in a clean checkout `npm ci && npm test; echo $?`. Also confirm with `gh pr list --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --search 102 --state open` that this work is in a single PR.\nPASS: the PR is on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test, its body contains `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`, `npm ci && npm test` exits 0 at the head, and the `test` workflow run for the head commit concluded success.\nFAIL: body lacks that text, the work is split over multiple PRs, `npm ci` or `npm test` fails locally, or the test workflow for the head SHA is missing, pending or failed.\n\n## Advisory\n- Also try a CRLF file and a file whose last line is valid but unterminated (should exit 0); report odd behaviour as notes, not failures.\n- Check that `package-lock.json` includes the new workspace (otherwise CI `npm ci` breaks) and that the bin file has a shebang and executable bit."}